Package: baxters-stereo-mix
Version: 0.1.0-1
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Baxters Lab <165753632+Baxterv5@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: libc6, libgcc-s1, libasound2t64, libpulse0, libgtk-3-0t64, libegl1,
 libwayland-client0, libwayland-egl1, libxkbcommon0, libx11-6, libxcb1,
 libdbus-1-3
Description: Baxters Stereo Mix — capture what the machine is playing
 Records system audio on Linux by capturing a PulseAudio monitor source, the
 equivalent of the Windows "Stereo Mix" device, and encodes to MP3 or WAV.
 .
 Depends were taken from the binary's DIRECT NEEDED entries plus the libraries
 eframe and winit dlopen at startup. ldd alone would have missed EGL, Wayland
 and xkbcommon entirely, producing a package that installs cleanly and then
 fails to open a window — the defect already found in Iris and Power Goo.
 .
 libmp3lame0 is deliberately NOT listed. It appears in ldd output only because
 libsndfile needs it; this binary imports zero LAME symbols dynamically and
 defines them internally, so its copy of LAME is static and comes from the
 package itself, not from the system.
